{"timestamp": "2026-08-11T16:22:43.223538+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages?beta=true', 'headers': {'anthropic-user-profile-id': <anthropic.Omit object at 0x0000026A9D8471D0>, 'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-861b548f-54a3-4926-95de-97ed7923ac98', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 512, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': [{'text': 'Review this generated raster image for classroom print use.\\n\\nReturn JSON with:\\n- verdict: \"accept\", \"flag\", or \"reject\"\\n- reasons: short concrete reasons\\n- correction_hint: one concise prompt correction if flagged or rejected\\n\\nAccept if the image is usable even if imperfect. Reject ONLY for unsafe or\\ninappropriate content. Flag all ordinary quality or constraint problems, including\\ngarbled or illegible labels, missing required content, must_not_show violations,\\nclearly low-quality output, or full-sentence caption/title text inside the image.\\nIf flagging caption/title text, set correction_hint to\\n\"remove all sentence text from the image\".\\nItems in must_show are REQUIRED. Their presence is never grounds for rejection.\\nFlag must_not_show violations, illegibility, or caption/sentence text.\\nDimension labels are allowed when required; area calculations or sums are not.\\n\\nPurpose: Draw a diagram step by step: (1) Place a large body of water at the bottom, label \\'Collection (ocean/lake)\\'. (2) Add the sun above, write \\'Sun\u2019s energy\\'. (3) Dr Lesson objective: Draw a clear labelled diagram of the water cycle showing evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection, and the movement of water, and describe the cycle using the diagram Teaching brief: Draw a diagram step by step: (1) Place a large body of water at the bottom, label \\'Collection (ocean/lake)\\'. (2) Add the sun above, write \\'Sun\u2019s energy\\'. (3) Draw an upward arrow from the water to the sky, label \\'Evaporation (water vapor)\\'. Explicitly note that water vapor is an invisible gas, so the arrow represents the vapor. (4) Draw cloud shapes at the top, label \\'Condensation (clouds)\\' and clarify that clouds are tiny liquid water droplets, not gas. (5) Draw a downward arrow from clouds to land and water, label \\'Precipitation (rain, etc.)\\'. (6) Add an arrow from land back to the ocean, label \\'Collection\\'. This block fulfills the visual requirement by showing labels and spatial arrangement.\\nMode: diagram\\nLabels required: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection, water cycle, water vapor\\n\\nMust show:\\n- Define evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection in the context of the water cycle\\n- Explain how the Sun\\'s energy drives evaporation\\n- Describe the sequence of processes that move water through the cycle\\n- Construct a labelled diagram showing the water cycle\\n\\nMust not show:\\n- transpiration\\n- sublimation\\n- groundwater flow\\n- water table\\n- detailed cloud formation beyond condensation\\n- atmospheric layers\\n\\nAlso flag if important labels are not legible in print.\\n', 'type': 'text'}, {'source': {'data': '', 'media_type': 'image/jpeg', 'type': 'base64'}, 'type': 'image'}]}], 'model': 'claude-haiku-4-5-20251001', 'stream': False, 'system': [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'You are a strict but practical image quality reviewer for educational materials. Return only the requested verdict.', 'cache_control': {'type': 'ephemeral', 'ttl': '5m'}}], 'tool_choice': {'type': 'any'}, 'tools': [{'name': 'final_result', 'description': 'The final response which ends this conversation', 'input_schema': {'properties': {'verdict': {'enum': ['accept', 'flag', 'reject'], 'type': 'string'}, 'reasons': {'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'type': 'array'}, 'correction_hint': {'default': '', 'type': 'string'}}, 'required':